Package: gnome-shell-extension-springdock
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, gnome-shell (>= 50~), gnome-shell (<< 52~)
Description: drag files onto dock icons to reach the app's window
 Springdock makes the icons in the GNOME Shell dock spring-loaded: while
 dragging a file (or other data) out of an application, holding it over
 another application's icon brings that application's window to the
 front, so the file can be dropped into it.
 .
 If the application has several windows, a row of live thumbnails
 appears next to the icon, and holding the drag over one raises that
 window. It is made for Ubuntu Dock and Dash to Dock, and can be
 switched on and off from Quick Settings.
